    "title": "WILD GAME - Wild Game Gourmet",
    "text": "Skip to content WILD GAME RECIPES Wild game is one of those foods that is obviously misunderstood by the people that don’t consume it, but is also often misunderstood by the ones who do.​For those that eat venison and other wild game, a great number of them usually have some quirky thing they think should be done in order to make the meat more palatable; Like soaking larger cuts in some random solution or adding weird starchy binders to their burgers.​While there certainly are things that can be done to alter flavor profiles, such as aging or marinating the meat, it’s mainly about mastering cooking and field care techniques. I”ll be covering these subjects in great detail with online tutorials sometime in the near future, so be sure to subscribe to my emails.​If you think of any questions in regards to cooking wild game meat, send me an email! VENISON RECIPESHere you'll find recipes for deer, antelope, elk, bison and more. GO TO RECIPES WILD PIG RECIPESOne of the most versatile meats out there! Pulled pork, Canadian bacon, sausages and cured hog recipes found here. GO TO RECIPES WATERFOWL RECIPES GO TO RECIPES WILD TURKEY RECIPESSimilar to your everyday turkey with some nuances GO TO RECIPES Subscribe Subscribe Loading Comments... Write a Comment... Email (Required) Name (Required) Website What is this? Report Ad",
